 {"id": "PEDS-C44-107", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Hyperpigmentation in 21-OH deficiency occurs because high ACTH also acts on the —", "opts": ["Melanin directly", "Glucocorticoid receptor", "Androgen receptor", "MSH receptor (similar structure)"], "ans": 3, "exp": "High ACTH also acts on melanocyte-stimulating hormone receptor (d/t similar structure) → hyperpigmentation. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-108", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "ACTH can stimulate the MSH receptor because of structural ___.", "opts": ["Structural similarity", "Identical secretion pulses", "Shared chromosome locus", "Common precursor of both receptors"], "ans": 0, "exp": "ACTH acts on MSH receptor d/t similar structure (of the peptides). (Book p207)", "type": "fill"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-109", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Newborn screening for 21-OH deficiency (CAH) estimates —", "opts": ["DHEA-S", "17-hydroxy progesterone (17-OHP)", "Cortisol", "Renin"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Newborn screening: estimation of 17-hydroxy progesterone (17-OHP) levels. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-110", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "The metabolite that accumulates upstream of the 21-OH block and is measured in newborn screening is ___.", "opts": ["Pregnenolone", "Androstenedione", "17-OHP", "11-deoxycortisol"], "ans": 2, "exp": "17-hydroxy progesterone (17-OHP) accumulates and is measured in newborn screening. (Book p207)", "type": "fill"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-111", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Lifelong replacement of aldosterone in CAH uses —", "opts": ["Hydrocortisone", "Desmopressin", "Aldosterone IV", "Fludrocortisone"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Lifelong replacement: aldosterone → fludrocortisone. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-112", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Cortisol replacement in CAH uses —", "opts": ["Hydrocortisone", "Fludrocortisone", "Prednisolone only", "Dexamethasone in neonates"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Lifelong replacement: cortisol → hydrocortisone. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-113", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "During MINOR stress (e.g., infection), hydrocortisone dose in CAH is increased to ___ times the maintenance dose.", "opts": ["10 times", "2–3 times", "1.5 times", "4–5 times"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Dose adjustment during stress: minor stress 2×–3× dose (infections). (Book p207)", "type": "fill"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-114", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "During MAJOR stress (e.g., surgery), the hydrocortisone dose in CAH is increased to —", "opts": ["6–8 times", "No change needed", "4–5 times", "2–3 times"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Major stress: 4×–5× dose (surgeries). (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-115", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Stress dosing of hydrocortisone is needed in CAH because of —", "opts": ["Fear of weight gain", "Reduced absorption during illness", "Drug interactions", "Increased requirement during stress"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Dose adjustment during stress d/t increased requirement. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-116", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Surgical correction of ambiguous genitalia in CAH (clitoroplasty) should be done within —", "opts": ["2–6 months", "6–12 months", "12–24 months", "Only after puberty"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Surgical correction of ambiguous genitalia: should be done within 2–6 months (clitoroplasty). (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-117", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "The surgical procedure named for correction of clitoromegaly in CAH is ___.", "opts": ["Urethroplasty", "Clitoroplasty", "Vaginoplasty only", "Labiaplasty only"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Surgical correction of ambiguous genitalia (clitoroplasty) within 2–6 months. (Book p207)", "type": "fill"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-118", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "A 46,XX newborn has clitoromegaly and labial fusion; at day 12 she develops shock with Na 122, K 6.4 mEq/L and hypoglycemia. Newborn screen shows high 17-OHP. Diagnosis —", "opts": ["17-α-hydroxylase deficiency", "3-β-HSD deficiency", "21-hydroxylase deficiency (salt-wasting CAH)", "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Ambiguous genitalia in a female + salt wasting (hyponatremia, hyperkalemia, shock) + high 17-OHP = 21-OH deficiency. (Book p207)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 12-day-old 46,XX neonate with clitoromegaly and fused labioscrotal folds presents with poor feeding, shock, Na 122 mEq/L, K 6.4 mEq/L. Newborn screen reports markedly elevated 17-OHP."},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-119", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Match the 21-OH deficiency feature with its mechanism:", "opts": ["A-1, B-3, C-4, D-2", "A-3, B-4, C-1, D-2", "A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4", "A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Correct pairs: Shock→Low aldosterone (salt wasting); Clitoromegaly→High androgens; Hyperpigmentation→ACTH acting on MSH receptor; Precocious puberty in males→High androgens. (Book p207)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Shock", "High androgens"], ["Clitoromegaly", "Low aldosterone (salt wasting)"], ["Hyperpigmentation", "High androgens"], ["Precocious puberty in males", "ACTH acting on MSH receptor"]]},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-120", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Odd one out (21-OH deficiency features):", "opts": ["Hypertension", "Shock", "Hyponatremia", "Hyperkalemia"], "ans": 0, "exp": "21-OH deficiency causes low BP/shock with salt wasting; hypertension belongs to 11-β-OH and 17-α-OH deficiency. (Book p207–208)", "type": "odd"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-121", "sec": "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "A child with known CAH on hydrocortisone develops chickenpox. The dose should be —", "opts": ["Halved", "Increased 2–3 times", "Kept the same", "Stopped temporarily"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Minor stress (infections): increase dose 2–3×. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-122", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "In 11-β-hydroxylase deficiency, the compound that accumulates and acts as a mineralocorticoid is —", "opts": ["Dehydroepiandrosterone", "Corticosterone", "11-deoxycorticosterone", "17-hydroxyprogesterone"], "ans": 2, "exp": "High 11-deoxycorticosterone (mineralocorticoid action) d/t enzyme deficiency. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-123", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "11-deoxycorticosterone accumulates in 11-β-OH deficiency because the block prevents its conversion to —", "opts": ["Aldosterone directly", "Cortisol", "Progesterone", "Corticosterone"], "ans": 3, "exp": "11-deoxycorticosterone → (11-β-OH) → corticosterone; the block piles up DOC. (Book p206–207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-124", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "The striking electrolyte/BP finding in 11-β-OH deficiency is —", "opts": ["Hypertension despite low aldosterone", "Hypotension with hyperkalemia", "Normotension always", "Hypertension with hyperkalemia"], "ans": 0, "exp": "High 11-deoxycorticosterone (mineralocorticoid action): HTN in spite of decreased aldosterone. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-125", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Hypertension with which feature points to 11-β-OH deficiency rather than renal disease?", "opts": ["Haematuria", "Ambiguous genitalia in a female", "Proteinuria", "Oedema"], "ans": 1, "exp": "11-β-OH deficiency: HTN (DOC) + androgen excess → ambiguous genitalia in females / precocious puberty in males. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-126", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Androgen effects of 11-β-OH deficiency include precocious puberty in males and ambiguous genitalia in —", "opts": ["Both", "Neither", "Females", "Males"], "ans": 2, "exp": "High androgens: precocious puberty (males), ambiguous genitalia (females). (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-127", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Hyperpigmentation in 11-β-OH deficiency is mediated by —", "opts": ["DOC on skin", "Androgens on skin", "Renin on melanocytes", "ACTH on MSH receptors"], "ans": 3, "exp": "High ACTH → hyperpigmentation (MSH-receptor cross-stimulation). (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-128", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Hormone profile in 11-β-OH deficiency shows —", "opts": ["High androgens, high ACTH, high DOC, low aldosterone/cortisol", "Low androgens, low ACTH, high aldosterone", "High aldosterone, low ACTH, high cortisol", "Normal steroids with high renin"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Clinical triad: high androgens + high ACTH + high 11-deoxycorticosterone, with decreased aldosterone and cortisol. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-129", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "A hypertensive 46,XX newborn has clitoromegaly, hyperpigmentation, Na 138, K 4.0 mEq/L, low cortisol and high ACTH. Diagnosis —", "opts": ["Maternal virilising tumour", "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "17-α-hydroxylase deficiency"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Ambiguous genitalia + HTN despite low aldosterone (DOC mineralocorticoid action) + hyperpigmentation = 11-β-OH deficiency. (Book p207)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 3-week-old 46,XX infant has clitoromegaly, hyperpigmented scrotal-like labia and BP above the 95th centile. Electrolytes are normal; cortisol is low, ACTH high."},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-130", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "In 11-β-OH deficiency, blood pressure is high \"in spite of\" decreased ___.", "opts": ["Decreased androgens", "Decreased renin", "Decreased aldosterone", "Decreased cortisol"], "ans": 2, "exp": "HTN in spite of decreased aldosterone — because accumulated 11-DOC has mineralocorticoid action. (Book p207)", "type": "fill"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-131", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "Both 21-OH and 11-β-OH deficiencies share —", "opts": ["Salt-wasting shock", "Hypertension", "Undervirilisation of males", "Androgen excess and hyperpigmentation"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Both shunt to increased androgens (virilisation) with high ACTH (hyperpigmentation); they differ in BP/DOC. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-132", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "The feature that best distinguishes 11-β-OH from 21-OH deficiency is —", "opts": ["Hypertension", "Clitoromegaly", "Hyperpigmentation", "Low cortisol"], "ans": 0, "exp": "11-β-OH: HTN (DOC excess); 21-OH: salt-wasting hypotension — both share virilisation and hyperpigmentation. (Book p207)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-133", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency causes hypertension through increased aldosterone.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — Aldosterone is low; HTN is d/t mineralocorticoid action of accumulated 11-deoxycorticosterone. (Book p207)", "type": "tf"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-134", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "In 11-β-OH deficiency the accumulated steroid just proximal to the block in the cortisol pathway is 11-deoxy___.", "opts": ["Pregnenolone", "Androstenedione", "Corticosterone", "Cortisol"], "ans": 2, "exp": "11-deoxycorticosterone (DOC) accumulates (mineralocorticoid action → HTN). (Book p207)", "type": "fill"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-135", "sec": "11-β-hydroxylase deficiency", "page": 207, "q": "A male with 11-β-OH deficiency may present with precocious puberty.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — High androgens cause precocious puberty in males. (Book p207)", "type": "tf"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-136", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "In 17-α-hydroxylase deficiency, cortisol is decreased and ACTH rises; the pathway that benefits is —", "opts": ["Aldosterone synthesis", "Androgen synthesis", "Cortisol synthesis", "Catecholamine synthesis"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Decreased enzyme → decreased cortisol → increased ACTH → increased increased aldosterone (aldosterone pathway favoured) + decreased testosterone. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-137", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "The BP abnormality of 17-α-hydroxylase deficiency is —", "opts": ["Labile BP", "Hypertension", "Hypotension", "Normal BP"], "ans": 1, "exp": "High aldosterone: hypertension. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-138", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "In 17-α-OH deficiency, testosterone is —", "opts": ["Normal", "Variable", "Decreased", "Increased"], "ans": 2, "exp": "17-α-OH deficiency → decreased testosterone (androgen pathway blocked). (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-139", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "A 46,XY newborn with 17-α-hydroxylase deficiency may show —", "opts": ["Normal male genitalia", "Precocious puberty", "Macro-orchidism", "Hypospadias with bifid scrotum"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Low androgens in males: undervirilization — hypospadias, bifid scrotum, delayed puberty; severe cases: ambiguous genitalia. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-140", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Male genital findings in 17-α-OH deficiency include hypospadias, bifid scrotum and delayed ___.", "opts": ["Puberty", "Dentition", "Walking", "Speech"], "ans": 0, "exp": "In males: undervirilization — hypospadias, bifid scrotum, delayed puberty; severe: ambiguous genitalia. (Book p208)", "type": "fill"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-141", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "In 17-α-OH deficiency, females are usually —", "opts": ["Salt-wasting", "Asymptomatic", "Virilised", "Hypertensive with hirsutism"], "ans": 1, "exp": "In females: usually asymptomatic. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-142", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Delayed/slow progression of puberty in 17-α-OH deficiency females is due to decreased —", "opts": ["Adrenal androgen receptor", "Ovarian follicles", "Aromatization of testosterone", "Gonadotropin reserve"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Slow/delayed progression of puberty d/t decreased aromatization of testosterone (decreased estradiol). (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-143", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Hyperpigmentation in 17-α-OH deficiency is due to —", "opts": ["High aldosterone", "Low cortisol directly", "High androgens", "High ACTH"], "ans": 3, "exp": "High ACTH: hyperpigmentation. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-144", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "A 15-year-old 46,XY patient raised as female has no breast development, primary amenorrhoea, absent uterus, hypertension and low testosterone. Diagnosis —", "opts": ["17-α-hydroxylase deficiency", "Androgen insensitivity syndrome", "21-hydroxylase deficiency", "5-α-reductase deficiency"], "ans": 0, "exp": "HTN (high aldosterone) + undervirilised 46,XY + delayed puberty (low estradiol from low androgen substrate) = 17-α-OH deficiency. (Book p208)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 15-year-old phenotypic female with 46,XY karyotype has hypertension, absent uterus, no thelarche, and very low testosterone and cortisol with high ACTH."},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-145", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Enzyme deficient in 3-β-HSD deficiency is 3-β-hydroxysteroid ___.", "opts": ["Dehydratase", "Dehydrogenase", "Decarboxylase", "Desaturase"], "ans": 1, "exp": "3-β-HSD = 3-β-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase deficiency. (Book p208)", "type": "fill"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-146", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "In 3-β-HSD deficiency, the hormones that DECREASE include cortisol, aldosterone, androgens and —", "opts": ["DHEA", "Progesterone", "Estradiol", "ACTH"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Decreased enzyme → decreased cortisol, decreased aldosterone, decreased androgens, decreased estradiol (with high ACTH). (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-147", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Low aldosterone in 3-β-HSD deficiency produces —", "opts": ["Hypertension with hypokalemia", "Normal electrolytes", "Isolated hypokalemia", "Low BP with hyponatremia and hyperkalemia"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Low aldosterone: decreased BP + hyponatremia + hyperkalemia. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-148", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "In 3-β-HSD deficiency, males show —", "opts": ["Undervirilization", "Precocious puberty", "Macro-penis", "Normal virilisation"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Low androgens in males: undervirilization. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-149", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Females with 3-β-HSD deficiency may show mild virilisation due to increased —", "opts": ["Estradiol", "Dehydroepiandrosterone", "Testosterone", "Androstenedione"], "ans": 1, "exp": "In females: mild virilization d/t increased DHEA (mild androgen) in the older child. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-150", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Mild virilisation of an older female child with 3-β-HSD deficiency includes acne, menstrual irregularities and —", "opts": ["Voice change always", "Frontal balding", "Hirsutism", "Clitoromegaly always"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Features: acne, hirsutism, menstrual irregularities (d/t increased DHEA). (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-151", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "DHEA, the mild androgen increased in 3-β-HSD deficiency, stands for ___.", "opts": ["Dehydroepiandrostenediol", "Dihydroepiandrosterone", "Deoxyepiandrosterone", "Dehydroepiandrosterone"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA) — a mild androgen upstream of the 3-β-HSD block. (Book p208)", "type": "fill"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-152", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Hyperpigmentation in 3-β-HSD deficiency results from —", "opts": ["High ACTH", "High DHEA", "Low aldosterone", "High estradiol"], "ans": 0, "exp": "High ACTH: hyperpigmentation. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-153", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "A salt-wasting 46,XY newborn has hypospadias and bifid scrotum; an older sister has acne and hirsutism. The enzyme deficiency —", "opts": ["17-α-OH", "3-β-HSD", "21-OH", "11-β-OH"], "ans": 1, "exp": "3-β-HSD: salt wasting + undervirilised males + mildly virilised older females (DHEA). (Book p208)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 46,XY newborn with hypospadias and bifid scrotum develops salt-wasting crisis; his 8-year-old sister has acne, hirsutism and menstrual irregularities with normal BP."},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-154", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "The diagnostic pointer table combines salt-wasting features with ___ status to differentiate enzyme deficiencies.", "opts": ["Serum ACTH", "Serum renin", "Serum androgen", "Serum cortisol"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Pointers for diagnosis use salt-wasting features and serum androgen to separate the enzyme deficiencies. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-155", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Salt-wasting features with HIGH serum androgens point to —", "opts": ["3-β-HSD deficiency", "11-β-OH deficiency", "17-α-OH deficiency", "21-OH deficiency"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Salt wasting + increased androgen = 21-OH deficiency. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-156", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Salt-wasting features with LOW serum androgens point to —", "opts": ["3-β-HSD deficiency", "21-OH deficiency", "11-β-OH deficiency", "17-α-OH deficiency"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Salt wasting + decreased androgen = 3-β-HSD deficiency. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-157", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Hypertension with HIGH serum androgens points to —", "opts": ["Aldosterone synthase deficiency", "11-β-OH deficiency", "21-OH deficiency", "3-β-HSD deficiency"], "ans": 1, "exp": "HTN + increased androgen = 11-β-OH deficiency. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-158", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Hypertension with LOW serum androgens points to —", "opts": ["21-OH deficiency", "3-β-HSD deficiency", "17-α-OH deficiency", "11-β-OH deficiency"], "ans": 2, "exp": "HTN + decreased androgen = 17-α-OH deficiency. (Book p208)", "type": "mcq"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-159", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Match the enzyme deficiency with its diagnostic pointer:", "opts": ["A-1, B-3, C-4, D-2", "A-3, B-4, C-1, D-2", "A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4", "A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Correct pairs: 21-OH→Salt wasting + high androgens; 3-β-HSD→Salt wasting + low androgens; 11-β-OH→HTN + high androgens; 17-α-OH→HTN + low androgens. (Book p208)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["21-OH deficiency", "Salt wasting + low androgens"], ["3-β-HSD deficiency", "HTN + high androgens"], ["11-β-OH deficiency", "HTN + low androgens"], ["17-α-OH deficiency", "Salt wasting + high androgens"]]},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-160", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Match the enzyme deficiency with its androgen-status genital effect:", "opts": ["A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2", "A-1, B-3, C-4, D-2", "A-3, B-4, C-1, D-2", "A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Correct pairs: 21-OH→Ambiguous genitalia (female); 11-β-OH→Precocious puberty (male); 17-α-OH→Undervirilization (male); 3-β-HSD→Mild virilization (female, DHEA). (Book p207–208)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["21-OH deficiency", "Precocious puberty (male)"], ["11-β-OH deficiency", "Undervirilization (male)"], ["17-α-OH deficiency", "Mild virilization (female, DHEA)"], ["3-β-HSD deficiency", "Ambiguous genitalia (female)"]]},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-161", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Odd one out (features of 17-α-hydroxylase deficiency):", "opts": ["Hypospadias", "Salt-wasting shock", "Delayed puberty in females", "Hypertension"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Salt-wasting belongs to 21-OH and 3-β-HSD deficiencies; 17-α-OH causes HTN with undervirilisation. (Book p207–208)", "type": "odd"},
 {"id": "PEDS-C44-162", "sec": "17-α-OH, 3-β-HSD deficiency and diagnostic pointers", "page": 208, "q": "Hyperpigmentation is a shared feature of 21-OH, 11-β-OH, 17-α-OH and 3-β-HSD deficiencies because ACTH is high in all.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — All CAH blocks lower cortisol → high ACTH → MSH-receptor cross-stimulation → hyperpigmentation. (Book p207–208)", "type": "tf"},
